    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195817": {
      "title": "Spring 2027: Adjunct (PT) Position for MGT363: Business Law",
      "description": "Department: Gettysburg College Location: Gettysburg, PA The Department of Management at Gettysburg College invites applications for an Adjunct Faculty position to teach one section of the undergraduate course MGT 363 Business Law. As per its course description, this course explores the “Legal environment of business and how law affects managerial decision-making; introduction to law of torts, business crimes, contracts, sales, product liability, consumer protection, bankruptcy, leases, formation of corporations and partnerships, employer-employee rights, environmental regulation, intellectual property, Uniform Commercial Code; examination of court systems, legal process; discussion of international business law, governmental regulation of business, constitutional issues relevant to business; use of case study method where appropriate.” The course meetings currently are scheduled for Wednesdays and Fridays from 1:10PM-2:25PM for the Spring 2027 semester. Classes must be taught in-person at the Gettysburg College campus. A relevant academic and/or professional background is required, which typically includes a Juris Doctorate (JD) degree. Previous teaching experience at the undergraduate level is preferred. Please submit a cover letter detailing your interest and qualifications, a curriculum vitae, and the names and contact information of two professional references. Review of applications begins immediately. Questions may be directed to Dr. Joseph Radzevick, Chair of the Department of Management, Gettysburg College, at jradzevi@gettysburg.edu."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193153": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Position in Health Sciences: Exercise physiology with specialization in strength and conditioning",
      "description": "Department: Gettysburg College: Health Sciences Location: Gettysburg, PA Gettysburg College invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in the Health Sciences Department beginning August 2027. Teaching responsibilities will include introductory and advanced undergraduate courses in exercise physiology , with an emphasis on scientific principles of strength and conditioning . The teaching load for this position will be five courses (or the laboratory equivalent) per year , and t he successful candidate will be responsible for sustaining a dynamic research program, advising health sciences majors, and actively participating in the governance of the department and college. This faculty member will also have the exciting opportunity to lead our efforts in becoming an accredited program through the Council on Accreditation of Strength and Conditioning Education (CASCE) to prepare students to become certified as strength and conditioning specialists. Candidates are required to have a Ph.D. (or be ABD) in exercise physiology or a closely related discipline and must currently hold a Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) certification or have acquired certification prior to start date . Preference will be given to candidates with prior undergraduate teaching experience, particularly experience teaching lecture and laboratory courses in the scientific principles of strength and conditioning , and a demonstrated commitment to effective and student-centered pedagogy. A research program is required , with a strong preference for scholarship centered on strength and conditioning. Please submit your electronic application using Interfolio , including a cover letter, curriculum vitae , a statement on teaching philosophy and approach, research statement, and the current email addresses for three professional references (at least one of whom can comment on your teaching ability). Professional references will be contacted through Interfolio to submit letters of recommendation electronically . Review of complete applications will begin on October 1 8 , 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries can be addressed to Dr. Amy Dailey, Professor and Chair of Health Sciences, at adailey@gettysburg.edu . Applicants can learn more about the College and the Department at https://www.gettysburg.edu/academic-programs/health-sciences/ ."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/193332": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Cognitive Psychology",
      "description": "Department: Gettysburg College: Psychology Location: Gettysburg, PA The Psychology Department at Gettysburg College invites applications for a tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level beginning August 202 7 in the area of Cognitive Psychology . Candidates will contribute courses to our rigorous undergraduate psychology curriculum and maintain a productive research program that can engage undergraduate research students. Teaching responsibilities will include 200-level courses in the candidate’s area of specialization, an upper-leve l laboratory course in the candidate’s research area, and may include introductory psychology , statistics or research methods. The teaching load is the equivalent of five courses over the academic year. Candidates will be expected to serve as academic advisors and participate in the governance of the department and college. Gettysburg’s Psychology Department offers students the options of a Bachelor of Arts (B.A.) or Bachelor of Science (B.S.) in psychology, and/or a neuroscience minor. Students pursuing the psychology major take engaging classes and conduct original self-guided or faculty-led research. The department includes nine tenured/tenure-track faculty and one lecturer, and graduates a pproximately 60 majors per year. We seek a colleague who has a genuine interest in teaching, research, and advising/mentoring undergraduate students. Candidate s should have a Ph . D . in the area of cognitive psychology. ABD will be considered if the degree will be completed prior to the start date . Candidates must demonstrate a commitment to mentoring and educating a broad range of undergraduate students . Candidates are expected to become high quality teachers and productive researchers, and Gettysburg College provides support through start-up funds, departmental and external faculty mentorship, department-specific tenure and promotion guidelines, internal professional development and travel funding, and family-friendly policies. The position has a dedicated multi-room laboratory space. Please submit your application through Interfolio. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a statement o n teaching philosophy and approach, a statement on research program and interests, and current email addresses for at least three professional references (at least one of whom can speak to your teaching effectiveness ). Applications and letters of recommendation received by October 16, 2026 will be given fullest consideration; however, submissions will continue to be reviewed until the position is filled . Inquiries can be addressed to Dr. Nathalie Goubet , Chair and Professor of Psychology at ngoubet@gettysburg.edu ."
    }
